.TH AD_GEN_OPS 1 "2026-09-01" "ad 2.0" "ad tools"
.SH NAME
ad_gen_ops \- generate a timed op file from old/new files + layer chain
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ad_gen_ops
<oldfile> <newfile> [--ad-layer=<name>]... [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ad_gen_ops
runs the ad pipeline
.RI ( compute \(-> postprocess \(-> pace )
and writes the timed ops to stdout. The output is V2 TSV format,
suitable for editing with
.B vim
(use
.IR scripts/vim/ad_ops_syntax.vim ).
.PP
This is the companion to
.BR ad_watch :
generate the initial ops with
.BR ad_gen_ops ,
then iterate on them in vim while
.B ad_watch
shows the result.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --help ", " -h
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BI --ad-layer= NAME
Add a layer to the postprocess chain. Layers run in argv order.
Repeatable.
.TP
.BI --ad-layer-path= DIR
Add a search path for layers.
.TP
.BI --delete-pacing= MODE
Delete pacing mode (char|word|rapid-eol|...).
.TP
.BI --insert-pacing= MODE
Insert pacing mode (char|word|accel|...).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Generate ops with reorder layer only:
.B ad_gen_ops old.py new.py --ad-layer=ad_layer_reorder > ops.tsv
.TP
Generate ops with multiple layers:
.B ad_gen_ops old.py new.py \\\\
.br
.B   --ad-layer=ad_layer_reorder \\\\
.br
.B   --ad-layer=ad_layer_indent_last > ops.tsv
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ad_watch (1),
.BR ad_tmux_watch (1),
.BR ad (1)
.PP
.I scripts/vim/ad_ops_syntax.vim
\(em vim syntax highlighting for op files
